{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_macros.html.j2" as m with context %}
{% block main %}
<section class="wrap page-head narrow">
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="lede">The short version: ThermoHammer is free, it comes as it is, and the leaderboard keeps only the runs it can trust.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap page-body narrow">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The apps and this site</h2>
    <p>ThermoHammer, the apps for Android, iPhone and Windows and this website, is free. It is provided as is, without warranty of any kind: we work to measure every device fairly, but we don't promise that every result is right, that the apps run on every device, or that the leaderboard is always there. A benchmark or a stress test keeps a device under full load, and the operating system stays in charge of its temperature limits; you run them at your own risk.</p>

    <h2>The leaderboard</h2>
    <p>A run you submit goes on the public leaderboard and on this site, with its measurements, the device model, its chip and its OS version. We may refuse a run, or remove one later, for example when it looks tampered with, couldn't have come from a real device of that model, or was scored by mistake. When the scoring changes, the board starts over on the new version; earlier runs stay on their pages, marked with their version.</p>

    <h2>AI models</h2>
    <p>The LLM test runs Google's Gemma 3 1B model. Gemma is provided under and subject to the Gemma Terms of Use found at <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms" rel="noopener">https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms</a>. By using ThermoHammer you agree not to use the Gemma model, or anything made from it, for any of the uses restricted by the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy at <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy" rel="noopener">https://ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy</a>.</p>
    <p>The AI section runs open models ({{ ai_models[:-1] | join(', ') }} and {{ ai_models[-1] }}), and the LLM test runs on llama.cpp on the CPU and the GPU. Each comes with its own licence.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>What the apps send and keep is in the <a href="{{ cfg.privacy_url }}" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>. For anything else, write to <a href="mailto:{{ cfg.support_email }}">{{ cfg.support_email }}</a>. We may change these terms; this page always has the current text.</p>
    <p class="fine">Last changed <time datetime="2026-11-23">23 Nov 2026</time>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
{{ m.cta_band('Run it on your own device.', 'Free on Google Play, the App Store and the Microsoft Store, with no account and no ads.') }}
{% endblock %}
